From ecfe8824a9c66bf280235dac3a79f183f3ca3c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:41:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] 02-rights candidate: verifier check VR and V7 replay of
 Grant writes

VR (a provisional name; workstream 10 holds V26) pairs each Grant
instruction with exactly one record of its kind. It replays each
Grant from its records (terms, escrow at the workshop ratio, seq,
quota, expiry, undo amounts) and compares the result with the Grant
account the transaction left. It fails undefined tags in the rights
block and malformed data, and also fails, until workstream 18's V0
lands, any instruction outside ABI v2. It also fails Grant accounts
that nothing explains and program accounts of no known kind. Missing
post-states or holding states are UNVERIFIABLE, never PASS. V7 rebuilds
holding writes by Grant instructions from the record amounts (settle
without a touch, then pay or credit). fclient and herald gain explicit
arms that ignore the new kinds.

The tests use unsigned placeholder transactions; nothing is signed or
derived. They inject an honest flow and ten dishonest variants into
the land fixture, which is put on the S1 path with 100 arms added to
one holding. They judge only the difference from that base and check
that the recorded fixtures yield no VR finding. With mutate-vr or
mutate-v7 the dependent tests stop detecting.

